## HARD — documented-standard violations

1. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLX/Screens/ModelsView.swift:248`** — `String(format: "%.0f%%", …)` violates AC-1's grep gate (`.paul/phases/v5-onboarding/05-04-PLAN.md:47`: "no `ByteCountFormatter`/`String(format:` outside Format.swift"; the 05-04 order log states "`String(format:` only in `Format.swift`"). The gate as written fails on any download row. (The plan's behaviour clause covers only byte/rate/duration, so the two clauses conflict; the mechanical check is still violated.)

2. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLX/Screens/BenchmarkView.swift:331-342`** (doc comment 325-326) — `BenchmarkCellRow` renders status as a word only, no glyph, contradicting DESIGN §4.3 ("every status is a glyph plus a word") and its own comment ("the status is a glyph plus a word … DESIGN.md §4.3"). Breaks on every cell row in Benchmark's "Cells" list and Results' unfinished-run list.

3. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLX/Screens/EnginesView.swift:181-185`** — disabled "Try Again" carries only an accessibility hint, no reason beside the control; DESIGN §4.6 requires the reason next to every job-starting control. Trigger: engine install failed and another job active (`canStartJob == false`) — the row shows no reason.

4. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLXKit/AppModel.swift:664`** — `.done` sets state from `summary?.ended == .restoreFailed`, but `summary` is cleared only for quickbench starts (`start()`), so it leaks across jobs. Trigger: a quickbench ends `restore_failed`, then any download/install completes — its `job.state` becomes `.failed` though it succeeded. No current UI reads `.failed` for those kinds; the stored state is wrong regardless.

5. **`ohyesmlx/server.py:584-591` vs `ohyesmlx/quickbench.py:1054-1058`** — two definitions of "newest wins" for the same `best.repo` resolution: `measured_at` string vs file mtime (violates "One definition of everything"; the docstrings disagree). The server-side copy is unreachable via production wiring (`summaries=quickbench.latest`, `server.py:1017`, already keyed by `best.repo`) and `tests/test_server.py:2312` reaches it only with a double that breaks that keying.

6. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLX/Screens/ResultsView.swift:162-167`** duplicates `AppModel.swift:265-271` — same "Left on disk … it was in use" template and rationale in two places (one-definition; tests pin only the AppModel copy).

7. **`app/Sources/OhYesMLX/Components/StatusGlyph.swift:36`** — glyph 9 pt; DESIGN §3 says 8 pt.

## JUDGEMENT — smells

8. Repeated switches over raw status strings in three places with inconsistent words: `BenchmarkView.swift:344` ("Pass") vs `ResultsView.swift:287` ("PASS"), `:298`, `:307`.
9. Duplicated install flow: `EnginesView.swift:71-76` (`startInstall`) vs `:192-197` (`retry`).
10. `AppModelTests.swift:1048` `waitUntilAsync` is a byte-for-byte duplicate of `waitUntil` (`:71-80`).

